multiplexing  serial communications interface The driver provides
support for boards that multiplex together up to four  communica‐
tions  interfaces.  Apparently the original maker of hardware us‐
ing this multiplexing protocol was AST.  Each device is the  mas‐
ter  device  for  up  to  four devices.  The kernel configuration
specifies these devices as slave devices of the device, as  shown
in  the  synopsis.  The slave ID given for each device determines
which bit in the interrupt multiplexing  register  is  tested  to
find  interrupts  for that device.  The specification for the de‐
vice is used to compute the base addresses for the subdevices and
the port for the interrupt multiplexing register.  The driver was
written by Roland McGrath and placed into the public domain.
